 !Example JETSPIN input file 24: long production run toward nozzle/collector
 !steady state, growing from a single nozzle bead.
 !
 !Electrostatic parameters are JETSPIN's canonical set (density charge
 !44000, collector distance 16 cm, external potential 30.02076857), shared
 !with Examples 3 and 6 and Test Cases 10, 15, 16-20.
 !
 !Rheology, air drag, insertion and removal are Test Case 23's;
 !initialization and print directives are Example 3's, so the jet grows from
 !a single nozzle bead instead of the pre-extended 400-element mesh used to
 !validate the refinement algorithm.
 !
 !This case is non-evaporative by definition. Its evaporative counterpart
 !is Test Case 25 (examples/input-25/input.dat), which is identical except
 !for the "evaporation" keyword. The split is deliberate: with evaporation
 !enabled this configuration reaches the code's own numerical instability
 !check at step 1078685 (stress NaN), while the non-evaporative one runs
 !cleanly, so keeping the two as separate inputs makes that controlled
 !comparison reproducible. See docs/examples/test-25.md.
 !
 !The dynamic-refinement threshold/every cadence is Example 5's
 !(0.4 cm / 1.d-3 s), not Test 23's tighter 0.10 cm / 1.d-5 s: growing this
 !jet from one bead with Test 23's cadence was found to compound a
 !nonphysical cross-section thinning across repeated refinement events.

 system 4
 integrator 4

 timestep 5.d-9
 final time 0.5d0
 print time 1.d-2
 seed 317

 print xyz 1.d-4
 print xyz maxnumber 400

 print list t x vn vc yz n angl lp rc
 printstat list t x vn yz n curn curc

 multiple step no
 dynamic refinement yes
 dynamic refinement start 2.5d-4
 dynamic refinement every 1.d-3
 dynamic refinement threshold 0.4d0
 dynamic refinement anchor 0.10d0

 airdrag yes
 airdrag airdensity     0.00121d0
 airdrag airviscosity   0.1511d0
 airdrag amplitude      1.d0
 airdrag airvelocity    -1000.d0

 inserting yes
 removing yes
 gravity yes

 points 1
 initial length 0.02
 nozzle velocity 0.282942121d0
 nozzle stress 0.d0
 yield stress   0.d0
 nozzle cross   0.005d0
 density mass   0.839253525d0
 density charge 44000.d0
 viscosity      20.d0
 elastic modulus 50000.d0
 collector distance 16.d0
 surface tension 21.133d0

 perturbation yes
 perturbation frequency 1.d4
 perturbation amplitude 1.d-3

 !Canonical JETSPIN potential; see the header note.
 external potential 30.02076857d0
 evaporation no
 evaporation polymer frac 0.06d0
 evaporation airviscosity 0.15d0
 evaporation temperature 293.15d0
 evaporation umidity 0.165d0
 evaporation bconstant 7.d0
 evaporation mconstant 0.1d0
 evaporation tconstant 1.d0
 evaporation diffusivity 0.242d0

 Finish
